{
  "id": "Compound::DB00977 - Gene::2099",
  "verbalization": "Ethinyl Estradiol is implicated in the regulation of Esr1 through a shared pathway involving Etonogestrel, a steroid hormone that binds to Esr1. The evidence suggests that Ethinyl Estradiol, through its interaction with Etonogestrel, indirectly influences Esr1 expression. This is supported by the observed causal relationships between Ethinyl Estradiol and various physiological responses, all of which are mediated by Etonogestrel. The lowest common ancestors of these entities—Therapeutic Steroid Hormone and 17-Hydroxy Steroid—highlight a common biological function in steroid hormone regulation, reinforcing the link between Ethinyl Estradiol and Esr1. The integration of these pathways suggests a mechanism where Ethinyl Estradiol may modulate Esr1 through Etonogestrel, potentially affecting downstream biological processes.",
